Here's your upgraded EEG Recorder. Here's what's new compared to your original script:
Recording system

Press R to start recording — it auto-creates a timestamped CSV file like eeg_recordings/eeg_20250329_143022.csv in the same folder as the script
Press R again to stop — it prints exactly how many samples were saved and the filename
Every raw sample (timestamp + ch1/ch2/ch3) gets written live as data comes in, so you never lose data even if you close the window

Visual warning system

Green ● SIGNAL OK — all channels below 80 µV, everything normal
Yellow ◆ CAUTION: >80µV — something's off, maybe movement artifact or loose electrode
Red ⚠ HIGH AMPLITUDE! — above 150 µV, the entire background starts blinking red so you can't miss it — could be dead battery, bad contact, or EMI
Dashed reference lines drawn on the graph at ±80 µV (yellow) and ±150 µV (red) so you can visually see where signals are relative to thresholds

Status bar at the bottom

Live/No Data dot with label
Actual sample rate readout
● REC blinking indicator with a running MM:SS timer and sample count while recording

How to use:

Run the script, verify graph is stable and green
Press R to start recording your session
Watch the warning colors — if it goes yellow/red, check your electrodes/battery
Press R again to stop, your CSV is ready for analysis
Press Q or close the window to quit

The thresholds (WARN_YELLOW = 80, WARN_RED = 150) are at the top — adjust them to whatever makes sense for your setup.